"""Installer-menu parameters, exposed on the "installer" child device.

Addresses are the parameter table of the Modbus RTU manual (0x0640-0x077A);
names, defaults and ranges are the technical handbook's parameter list (§5.3).
Scaling was checked against a real unit's raw read-back: temperatures,
pressures and rps are x0.1, fan/compressor/damper percentages x0.01, times and
codes x1.

Parameters that already have an entity of their own (setup or configuration)
are not repeated here. Registers above 1900 (PT05-PT11 test relays, display
backlight/LED/icon PH31-PH35, external damper PA61/PA62) are not polled: none
of them is used on the HRDS+ and their readability is unverified, and one bad
address would push a whole block onto the slow per-register fallback. Deliberately left out altogether: passwords (PSd*),
PH15 "restore factory defaults" and PH18 "clear alarm history".

Each row: (code, register, kind, factor, min, max, unit, English name,
German name, enabled by default).

kind: "n" writable number, "s" writable 0/1 switch, "r" read-only sensor.
Read-only rows are things that must not be changed from Home Assistant: the
serial/CAN link settings (changing them cuts the connection), refrigerant and
pressure-probe calibration, the compressor safety-time bypass and test mode.
Rows the HRDS+ does not use (greyed out in the handbook: return fan, air
quality, heat-recovery defrost, external damper, rotary exchanger, expansion
I/O) are created but disabled by default.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

T = 0.1  # temperature, pressure, rps
P = 0.01  # fan / compressor / damper percentage

